<!-- BRAND05 foreground — the TroubaStage mark. Generated from
     docs/brand/dist/troubastage-adaptive-foreground.svg via this pipeline:
       1. picosvg  — bakes GROUP transforms into path geometry (s2v alone mis-scaled the mark
          off-canvas). Also intersects the source's two <clipPath>s into path geometry, which is
          why 41 source paths become 50 and no <clip-path> appears here (BRAND05 trap #2 — a
          non-issue *because* picosvg absorbed it; a pipeline swap could bring it back).
       2. docs/brand/tools/bake_gradients.py — bakes every gradientTransform MATRIX into the
          gradient's own userSpaceOnUse coordinates. s2v silently DROPS gradientTransform, which
          left six gradients degenerate (1-unit / zero-length axes) — flat fills where ramps were
          intended.
       3. docs/brand/tools/resolve_obb.py — resolves the objectBoundingBox stroke gradients (gMono/gRim/gWhite)
          to per-path viewport coordinates (s2v turns objectBoundingBox-on-stroke into NaN).
          The objectBoundingBox skew on non-square bboxes is unrepresentable in VectorDrawable
          (userSpaceOnUse isolines only), so endpoints are mapped exactly and the skew — on
          sub-perceptual near-white highlights — is dropped deliberately.
     gRule DELIBERATE CHANGE (trap #1): the staff-rules falloff is an OVAL radial
     (gradientTransform scale(1,0.55)). VectorDrawable radials are circular-only, so it is rendered
     as a circle centred on the staff (centerY=640, gradientRadius=235 = the oval's vertical
     semi-axis, which governs the rules' softness). Verified against the source SVG side by side.
     No <monochrome>: a legible one-colour "Stage" silhouette is authoring work, so themed-icon
     users fall back to the standard icon — a recorded decision. -->
